  "flavor": {
    "name_bank_key": "khordurn",
    "phonemic_palette": "Khordurn (Durnkad central dialect): hard consonant frames (k/g/d/t/b/p, clusters dr/br/gr/kr/thr/rd/rg/rk/nd, geminates kk/gg/dd/mm/nn) around soft open vowels (a/o/u, some e/i); short, heavy CVC syllables with initial stress - rhythmic, like hammer-strokes, the soft vowels rolling a lilt between the hard beats.",
